{
  "name": "D068 - Judge gate (accepted / needs_review)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ANTI-OVER-FLAGGING (owner rule, load-bearing)\n\nThe previous attempt \"flagged every fucking thing\". This gate is\nbuilt so that CANNOT happen:\n\n- Two outcomes only: **accepted** and **needs_review**.\n  There is no flag branch. Low confidence -> **unreviewed**, never\n  a flag. A flag fired wrongly a thousand times is worse than no flag.\n- The gate is an AND: `confidence >= {{THRESHOLD}}` **and**\n  `verdict == \"pass\"`. Either miss -> needs_review.\n- needs_review is a QUEUE, not a finding. Nothing downstream may\n  render it as an alert, a hit, or evidence of anything.\n\n`{{THRESHOLD}}` default **0.7**; overridable per batch via\n`body.threshold`.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "051a9e40-0000-0000-0000-00000000002d",
      "name": "STICKY - Anti-over-flagging",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## TOP-JUDGE SLOT - HIGH-STAKES ITEMS ONLY\n\nInterview B added a HIGHEST tier above the free-model judges:\nthe **Claude SDK / long-lived token**, used ONLY for the most\nconsequential decisions - never on every chunk.\n\nWiring it is a SEPARATE deploy task, deliberately NOT done here:\n- `n8n-nodes-claude-cli` (verified real, MIT, but ~6 weeks old,\n  single maintainer, 0 stars) needs the `claude` binary INSIDE the\n  n8n container -> a **custom n8n image via Coolify**, same shape as\n  the existing custom graphiti-mcp image.\n- Auth = `claude setup-token` long-lived token in Coolify env\n  storage (never git), or a read-only `~/.claude` mount.\n- **ToS caveat, raised by the package's own author**: driving a\n  Pro/Max subscription through recurring automation may conflict\n  with Anthropic's subscription terms. **PENDING OWNER RULING** -\n  do not enable on a schedule before that decision.\n\nThe disabled `TOP-JUDGE SLOT` No-Op node marks the insertion point.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "051a9e40-0000-0000-0000-00000000002e",
      "name": "STICKY - TOP-JUDGE SLOT (pluggable, pending owner ruling)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OPTIONAL: COUNCIL PATTERN (reserved, NOT built)\n\nReference: **template-12316** \"OpenRouter council\"\n(n8n.io/workflows/12316, extracted in Stage 3).\n\n3 stages: N models answer independently -> responses are\n**anonymized** and cross-ranked by the models themselves ->\na chairman model synthesizes the verdict.\n\nInvoke it ONLY when this single-judge gate is inconclusive on a\nhigh-stakes chunk - never per chunk (cost/rate-limit sanity).\nThe anonymize-before-ranking step is the de-biasing detail worth\ncarrying over verbatim if this is ever built.\n\nAlso parked as a cheap pre-filter candidate:\n`bespoke-minicheck` via Ollama (awesome-hallucination-detection.json).",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "051a9e40-0000-0000-0000-00000000002f",
      "name": "STICKY - Optional council pattern",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        520,
        -640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## PLACEHOLDERS\n\n- `{{PORTKEY_BASE_URL}}` / `{{PORTKEY_CONFIG_ID}}` on credential\n  **PORTKEY_GATEWAY (placeholder)** (`openAiApi` type)\n- `{{PORTKEY_JUDGE_MODEL}}` - the SECOND model; it MUST NOT be the\n  same model that produced the classification.\n- `{{PORTKEY_FIXER_MODEL}}` - stronger tier for the auto-fix retry.\n- `{{THRESHOLD}}` - default 0.7.\n\n## CANNIBALIZED FROM\n- **template-15229** -> the IF-gate wiring: one confidence check\n  branching to a needs-review path vs a silent continue.\n  (Its `@easybits/...` extractor node was discarded - native\n  Structured Output Parser covers it.)\n- **template-12316** -> council pattern (reference only).\n- **native docs** Basic LLM Chain, Auto-fixing + Structured parsers,\n  IF v2.3, Loop Over Items v3.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "051a9e40-0000-0000-0000-000000000030",
      "name": "STICKY - Placeholders + source attribution",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1020,
        -640
      ]
    },
